\subsection{\auctex Folding Support}
To enable folding of noweb macros they must be present in the variable
\texttt{TeX-fold-macro-spec-list}. Folding of noweb environment would be
supported by adding these to \texttt{TeX-fold-env-spec-list}. These will
apply to all \auctex modes unless the mode-specific spec-list variable
is used instead (e.g. \texttt{LaTeX-fold-env-spec-list} would limit the
folding support for noweb environments to \LaTeX{}-specific modes enhanced
by \auctex).

\subsection{\reftex Label Support}
\label{sec:label support}
<<>>=

@ 

The \reftex manual states that [[reftex-label-alist]] is bound to an
association list with infromation about the label and reference commands
used to refer to sections (and environments). Seeing the
[[reftex-label-alist-builtin]] below, I can understand that there is
support for implicit and explicit environments: with an implicit
environment being a section (\`{a} la \html; ``implicit
environments'' may not be a concept in \LaTeX{}, but such nesting is how I
conceive of hierarchical structuring in \LaTeX{} as it actually is in
\html).

